<h1>Eric Su</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 21st District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Republican.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.teamericsu.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (teamericsu.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>His campaign site names high property taxes, education quality and high health care costs as his three focus issues, and says he supports property tax relief, expanded access to affordable health care and mental health services, career and technical education, and fair wages that do not harm small businesses. He told the Riverside-Brookfield Landmark in 2025 he proposes a health savings match for low-income families and learn-and-earn labs linking high school students with employers.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Fitness trainer and small business owner for more than 20 years, a Purdue University graduate and former election judge who lives in North Riverside.</p>
